/* func_level_0_8007B020 (0x8007B020, level_0_artisans_home overlay).
 *
 * Balloonist cutscene tick — the per-frame update half of gamestate 0xC
 * (func_level_0_8007CFC0 is the draw half). Dispatches on the substate word
 * D_800777E8 through an 8-entry jump table (jtbl_8007AA3C):
 *   0  approach: swing the camera round to the balloonist over 0x60 frames,
 *   1  dialogue: pad-driven page/roster menu (D_800777F4 submode),
 *   2  board:    fly Spyro to the balloon over 0x66 frames,
 *   3  lift off: raise the balloon (Z) for 0x80 frames, then snapshot the
 *                actor into D_80071E9C and swap the 0x4000-byte scratch bank,
 *   5  cruise:   interpolate the camera along the flight path (0x100 frames),
 *   6  descend:  lower the balloon for 0x80 frames,
 *   7  land:     ease Spyro out of the balloon, then hand the frame back to
 *                gamestate 0 (func_80058C7C).
 * Substate 4 is the "wait for the level stream" state and falls straight
 * through to the epilogue.  Identical body in the six hub overlays.
 *
 * Blocks are addressed through their splat symbols declared as incomplete
 * arrays and indexed with constants, so cse's related_value derives the
 * sibling offsets off one held base (A36) — that is what produces the
 * original's `lw 0(s0)` / `lw -0x18(s0)` pairs off D_80077838 and the
 * `addiu a1,s1,0x20` / `addiu s1,s1,0x14` derivations off D_800777EC.
 * A pointer local (`int *rot = D_80077838; rot[-6]`) is the trap here: it
 * gives the pseudo a qty_const and B-i rule 1 folds every nonzero offset
 * back to absolute. Dropping the pointer locals for direct constant-index
 * access on the SAME symbol was worth 42 insns on its own.
 *
 * ============================ PARK 2026-08-19-3 ============================
 * DECODE COMPLETE and much closer than the 2026-08-06-3/2026-08-18 notes said.
 * Re-measured with the register-ANCHORED shape diff (§C: a masked figure only
 * answers "is the decode right?"):
 *      2020 orig insns vs 2008 built, MISMATCH 230 over 114 regions anchored,
 *      67 over 45 with register names masked entirely.
 * So ~163 of the 230 are pure register naming, and 38 regions change length.
 * Three things fixed this session (they took it from 473/201 anchored):
 *  - FRAME: the stack vectors are PSY-Q VECTOR/SVECTOR (16/8 bytes), not int[3].
 *    int vecA[4] / short ang[4] x6 + a dead short pad[4] reproduces sp-0x88
 *    exactly (0x10,0x20,0x28,0x38,0x48,0x58 with the 0x68 hole).
 *  - PER-ARM LOCALS: every switch arm gets its own braced block with its own
 *    scalars (t/n/k/sn/cn/cz/yaw/z/i/step). One shared set across seven arms is
 *    what produced the whole-function rotation the old note blamed on the held
 *    bases: 473 -> 251 anchored from this change alone.
 *  - 0x80076E1C..0x80076E20 is THREE scalars, not an array: the array form gives
 *    a held base (`addiu s0,s0,28188`) where the original re-emits `lui;lh
 *    %lo(sym+K)` at all nine sites. The missing splat symbol at +2 is reachable
 *    as `extern short D_80076E1E;` (the linker
 *    then gets D_80076E1C+2, byte-identical to the original reloc).
 *    NB the old wip did not even LINK -- it referenced an undefined D_80076E1E.
 *
 * What is left, biggest first:
 *  R1  @8007B2B0, 7 insns - the cross-jump asymmetry. **Root-caused off the
 *      gcc 2.7.2 source 2026-08-29, and the old "no source form addresses this"
 *      verdict is WRONG: the merge is CONTENT-based and a source dial removes
 *      it. Do not re-derive any of this.**
 *      MECHANISM. `cross_jump` runs exactly ONCE (toplev.c:3142,
 *      `jump_optimize (insns, 1, 1, 0)`, after reload -- the other four calls
 *      pass cross_jump=0), so every label `do_cross_jump` creates is NEW.
 *      Two merge paths, and only one of them is uid-gated:
 *        (a) jump.c:1985 `if (INSN_UID (JUMP_LABEL (insn)) < max_uid)` guards
 *            the jump_chain walk that pairs TWO JUMPS TO THE SAME LABEL
 *            (`find_cross_jump (insn, target, 2, ...)`), so a label born in
 *            this pass can never pair two jumps; but
 *            `get_label_before` REUSES a pre-existing label when one already
 *            sits there, and the inner if/else join label from expand does sit
 *            there -- which is why our build still gets path (a).
 *        (b) jump.c:1978 `find_cross_jump (insn, JUMP_LABEL (insn), 1, ...)`
 *            compares the block with the insns BEFORE the target label. No uid
 *            gate. This is the path that legitimately merges the two ELSE
 *            blocks (arm1's `j` -> the `subu` run that falls into the join),
 *            and it is the merge the ORIGINAL has.
 *      `find_cross_jump` scans backward, decrementing `minimum` per matching
 *      insn (2 for path (a), 1 for path (b)) and merging when it reaches 0, so
 *      differentiating an insn 3+ back from the jump does NOT stop a merge --
 *      only the last one or two insns count, and those are `addu v0,v0,v1` /
 *      `sra v1,t1,0xd`, which cannot be respelled.
 *      MEASURED DIAL (2026-08-29, compile-only shape diff): a block-scoped
 *      `int k;` inside the `t >= 0x48` branch makes arm3's accumulator a
 *      SEPARATE pseudo, it wins `a0` instead of `v0`, the two then-blocks stop
 *      being register-identical and **the merge disappears -- orig[162..170]
 *      come out inline and correct** (running offset at that point goes
 *      -7 -> 0). Cost: the ELSE blocks stop being identical too, so path (b)
 *      dies with it (+10 insns) -- net 230/-12 -> 237/+5, byte-identical words
 *      102 -> 118. Symmetric splits (both branches) are byte-identical to that.
 *      SO THE OBJECTIVE IS EXACT: make the two THEN blocks differ while the two
 *      ELSE blocks stay register-identical. Since with one shared `k` both
 *      pairs are identical, that needs arm3's `k` to reach `v0` (the original's
 *      register) while still being a distinct pseudo -- i.e. this is now an
 *      ALLOCATION problem (R3), not a structural one, and R3 must be fixed
 *      first. Note the baseline ALREADY has arm3's k in `a0` (0x454
 *      `addu a0,v0,v1`) against the original's `v0`, and `sn` in s1 against
 *      s0, so the arm's whole quantity map is off before R1 is even reached.
 *      RULED OUT and not worth re-testing: differentiating the `lw D_80077818`
 *      by an equal-address alias symbol (`(&D_80077814)[1]`, byte-identical
 *      reloc) -- the mismatch lands 4 insns back, `minimum` is already 0 by
 *      then and a 3-insn tail still merges.
 *  R2  held-base vs absolute addressing on D_800777EC / D_800777F0 /
 *      D_800777F4 / D_80077838. LARGELY CLOSED 2026-09-01 -- see the SCALAR
 *      ALIAS entry below; what is left of it is the shared-s0 cluster (R6).
 *  R3  a0<->v1 / v0<->v1 caller-saved rotations inside arms (44+38+20+17 sites).
 *  Budget it as one more focused session; the byte prize is 8,096 B x 6 hub
 *  overlays plus the level_1/3/7/8 near-clones = 80,960 B.
 *
 * ---- 2026-09-01: 230/114/offset -12  ->  161 over 85 regions, offset +6 ----
 * (register-anchored, immediate-masked compile-only shape diff, §D 2b.  All
 *  four levers are one-liners; none of them needed a permuter.)
 *
 *  LEVER A -- THE SCALAR ALIAS, and it is the general form of §B16 REVERSED.
 *      B16 says an incomplete-array alias cast-deref buys the REGISTER form.
 *      The complement is what this function needed: a plain `extern int X;`
 *      DECL is a `(mem (symbol_ref))` with the address inline, so it always
 *      comes out `lui %hi / lw %lo` and cse can never hold a base for it.  Two
 *      C names at ONE address therefore give the two forms per site, which is
 *      exactly what "the original uses BOTH forms for every one of these
 *      symbols" needs.  Declare the alias in the overlay's
 *      `config/overlays/<ovl>.undefined_syms.auto.txt` (a plain
 *      `NAME = 0xADDR;` line; `gen-syms-ld` PROVIDEs it, so an unused alias
 *      costs nothing) -- the main-EXE equivalent is symbol_addrs.txt with
 *      `allow_duplicated:True`.  Measured, each from the same baseline:
 *        D_800777F4 scalar      230 -> 210/107, offset -12 -> -3
 *        D_80077838 scalar      230 -> 215/107, offset -9
 *        both together          230 -> 195/100, **offset 0** (length-exact)
 *        D_800777F0 scalar      makes it WORSE except at one site (see below)
 *        D_800777EC scalar      blanket is much worse (325/150); per-arm only
 *      So it is per-SITE, and the cheap way to find the sites is to bisect the
 *      swap over source LINE RANGES against the shape diff, not to reason about
 *      it: three bisections (F4 reverted in lines 575-600, F0 scalar at exactly
 *      one line, EC scalar in lines 370-430) were worth another 195 -> 170.
 *  LEVER B -- D_80076E1E deserves a REAL SYMBOL.  The old
 *      `#define D_80076E1E (*(short *)((char *)&D_80076E1C + 2))` is an
 *      INDIRECT_REF, so it force_regs a base and cse holds it; the original
 *      re-emits `lui/lh %lo` at all nine sites.  Adding `D_80076E1E =
 *      0x80076E1E;` to the overlay's undefined_syms and declaring
 *      `extern short D_80076E1E;` is worth 195/100 -> 186/96.  General rule:
 *      a missing splat symbol reached by pointer arithmetic is a HELD BASE in
 *      disguise -- add the symbol rather than the cast.
 *  LEVER C -- the loop compare constant is HOISTED by the original.  The
 *      `D_800758D0[i] == 2` scan loop has `li a0,2` in the ORIGINAL's preheader
 *      and re-materialises nothing inside; ours emitted `li v0,2` per
 *      iteration.  Assigning it to one of the function's shared int locals
 *      (`k = 2;` above the loop, then `== k`) reproduces the hoist: 170 -> 165.
 *      This is §B10 in reverse -- there the ORIGINAL re-materialises inline and
 *      we hoist; check the direction before calling it a wall.
 *  LEVER D -- `if (a && b) ... else if (c && d)` vs a nested inner `if`.
 *      The five-arm `k == N` / global-test chain that picks the 0x21..0x25
 *      submode: the original branches BOTH failing conditions to the NEXT arm's
 *      compare and fills each branch delay slot with that arm's compare
 *      constant.  A nested `if (k == N) { if (g == 0) ... }` threads the inner
 *      failure straight to the join instead and leaves four `nop`s; a flat
 *      sequential `if` chain re-tests every arm (offset +14).  Only the
 *      `&&` spelling reproduces it: 165 -> 161.
 *
 * ---- What is left (161 insns over 85 regions) ----------------------------
 *  R1  unchanged -- the cross-jump asymmetry above, still -7 for ~1,850 insns.
 *  R6  THE SHARED s0 BASE, and it is now the single biggest structural item
 *      (11 sites x 1 insn).  The original materialises `s0 = &D_800777F4` ONCE
 *      (orig[569] `lui s0,0x8007; addiu s0,s0,30708`) and then reads and writes
 *      the whole D_800777EC/F0/F4 triple through it across several switch arms
 *      as `0(s0)`, `-4(s0)`, `-8(s0)` -- i.e. a callee-saved base with NONZERO
 *      offsets, which is precisely the §B-i rule 1 fold NOT happening.  Ours
 *      emits a fresh `lui/addiu` per derived address (`D_800777F4[-1]` gives
 *      `lui a0; addiu a0,a0,-4; lw v0,0(a0)`).  RULED OUT this session:
 *      respelling the triple as one array everywhere (`EC[0]` -> `F4[-2]`,
 *      `F0[0]` -> `F4[-1]`, scalar -> `F4[0]`) is 218/114/+8, much worse --
 *      gcc does not share the base just because the source names one array.
 *      The untried idea is A200's empty `do { } while (0)` barrier between the
 *      base's first use and the offset accesses, which is the only known way to
 *      stop the constant equivalence that folds `(plus base K)`.
 *  R3  the caller-saved rotations, unchanged and still the bulk of the count.
 *  Sites still worth a look, from the region list: orig[103]/[105] (a 2-insn
 *  D_8007784C read scheduled 2 early), orig[1369-1388] and orig[1737-1749]
 *  (store/load position shuffles), orig[1974-1982] (`sw s0,0(s1)` position).
 */

